[I] Tool for generating random C programs

[T] Csmith is a tool that generates random C programs that statically and
[T] dynamically conform to the C99 standard, developed at the University of
[T] Utah. It is used to find compiler bugs through differential testing, by
[T] comparing the output of programs compiled with different compilers or
[T] options.

[U] https://github.com/csmith-project/csmith/

[A] Csmith Authors
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

